            <div xml:id="d466">

                <pb facs="0557" n="459" xml:id="pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3436: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1920-08-08T11:23:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1920-08-02T00:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received August 8, 1920—11:23
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>215. Presidential mandate dissolves all branches of the Anfu Club and also the
                    15th division of the regular Army which assisted Tuan. Tsao Kun and Chang Tso
                    Lin are now in Peking conferring with the President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
